{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":77757,"num_turns":3,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"9c2eed08-d02b-5d7d-af3b-fb152e0ad051","total_cost_usd":0.69598,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14617,"cache_read_input_tokens":9713,"output_tokens":7787,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14617,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2337,"cache_read_input_tokens":9713,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4904,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4904},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":4442,"outputTokens":19,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.004536999999999999,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-fable-5":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":7787,"cacheReadInputTokens":9713,"cacheCreationInputTokens":14617,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.691443,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-fable-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"reviewer_participant_id\":\"actor:dependence-free-batch-j1-reviewer-fable-44\",\"reviews\":[{\"case_id\":\"case:eb93048bfef98eab102f\",\"verdict\":\"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope\",\"bounded_statement\":null,\"root_cause\":null,\"issue_class\":null,\"evidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"The data description names landform_id as the independent-unit column and states each rock glacier was surveyed exactly once, with no landform appearing twice among the 25 rows.\",\"observed_value\":\"25 rows, 25 distinct landforms, one survey each\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":6,\"end_line\":8,\"quoted_text\":\"No\\nlandform was resurveyed and none appears twice, so the file holds 25 rows and\\n25 distinct landforms.\"},{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":10,\"end_line\":11,\"quoted_text\":\"One row is: one rock glacier, surveyed once and summarised by a single mean creep velocity\\nIndependent unit column: landform_id\"}]},{\"description\":\"By direct inspection of the input CSV, the 25 data rows carry landform_id values RG-01 through RG-25 with zero duplicates, so no independent unit contributes more than one row to the row-independent procedure.\",\"observed_value\":\"25 unique landform_id values (RG-01..RG-25), 12 micaschist rows and 13 orthogneiss rows\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"data/input.csv\",\"start_line\":1,\"end_line\":2,\"quoted_text\":\"landform_id,bedrock_class,crest_elevation_m,mean_slope_deg,creep_velocity_cm_yr\\nRG-01,micaschist,2685,17.4,24.7\"},{\"path\":\"data/input.csv\",\"start_line\":26,\"end_line\":26,\"quoted_text\":\"RG-25,orthogneiss,2678,18.9,16.0\"}]},{\"description\":\"The workflow enforces uniqueness of the independent-unit column before computing any statistics, raising an error if any landform_id repeats; the Welch t-test therefore runs only on data guaranteed to have one row per unit.\",\"observed_value\":\"uniqueness guard on landform_id precedes stats.ttest_ind\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":39,\"end_line\":41,\"quoted_text\":\"ids = [row[UNIT_COL] for row in rows]\\n    if len(set(ids)) != len(ids):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"landform_id must be unique: one row per landform\\\")\"},{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":62,\"end_line\":62,\"quoted_text\":\"result = stats.ttest_ind(x, y, equal_var=False)\"}]},{\"description\":\"The report's design section and selected result accurately claim one row per landform and 25 independent observations, matching the data.\",\"observed_value\":\"reported n = 12 + 13 = 25 equals the number of distinct landforms\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":5,\"end_line\":7,\"quoted_text\":\"Each row of `data/input.csv` is one rock glacier, surveyed once. No landform\\ncontributes more than one row, so the 25 velocity values are 25 independent\\nobservations.\"},{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":25,\"end_line\":25,\"quoted_text\":\"[selected-result] Welch two-sided t-test: micaschist-hosted rock glaciers creep 8.00 cm/yr faster than orthogneiss-hosted ones (24.00 vs 16.00 cm/yr; t = 4.06, df = 19.8, p < 0.001, Cohen's d = 1.65), one row per landform.\"}]}],\"counterevidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"Searched for any sign that an independent unit enters the procedure repeatedly (duplicate landform_id values, resurveys, row expansion or replication in the workflow) and found none; the reported group sizes, means, SDs, and Welch statistics (n = 12 vs 13, 24.00 vs 16.00 cm/yr, SD 5.63 vs 4.01, t = 4.06, df = 19.8, p < 0.001, d = 1.65) all reproduce from the 25-row CSV under one-row-per-landform analysis, leaving no unexplained inflation of effective sample size.\",\"observed_value\":\"hand recomputation from data/input.csv reproduces all reported statistics; no duplication mechanism exists in workflow/analysis.py\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":13,\"end_line\":14,\"quoted_text\":\"| micaschist | 12 | 24.00 | 5.63 |\\n| orthogneiss | 13 | 16.00 | 4.01 |\"},{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":21,\"end_line\":23,\"quoted_text\":\"Difference in means (micaschist - orthogneiss): 8.00 cm/yr\\nt = 4.06, Welch-Satterthwaite df = 19.8, p < 0.001\\nCohen's d (pooled SD) = 1.65\"},{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":48,\"end_line\":52,\"quoted_text\":\"def velocities(label):\\n        return np.array(\\n            [float(row[VALUE_COL]) for row in rows if row[GROUP_COL] == label],\\n            dtype=float,\\n        )\"}]}],\"falsification_attempt\":\"I attempted to demonstrate the issue by (1) scanning all 25 landform_id values in data/input.csv for duplicates (none: RG-01 through RG-25 each appear exactly once), (2) checking the workflow for any code path that could replicate rows or aggregate repeated surveys into the test (there is none; a guard raises ValueError on duplicate IDs before stats.ttest_ind is called), and (3) recomputing the group counts, means, standard deviations, Welch t statistic, Welch-Satterthwaite df, and Cohen's d by hand from the CSV. All recomputed values (n = 12/13, means 24.00/16.00, SD 5.63/4.01, t = 4.06, df = 19.8, d = 1.65, p < 0.001) match the report, so the selected result is consistent with exactly one entry per independent unit and the issue could not be demonstrated.\",\"cross_case_evidence_used\":false,\"unresolved_material_questions\":[],\"self_reported_confidence\":\"high\"}]}","structured_output":{"reviewer_participant_id":"actor:dependence-free-batch-j1-reviewer-fable-44","reviews":[{"case_id":"case:eb93048bfef98eab102f","verdict":"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope","bounded_statement":null,"root_cause":null,"issue_class":null,"evidence_atoms":[{"description":"The data description names landform_id as the independent-unit column and states each rock glacier was surveyed exactly once, with no landform appearing twice among the 25 rows.","observed_value":"25 rows, 25 distinct landforms, one survey each","source_spans":[{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":6,"end_line":8,"quoted_text":"No\nlandform was resurveyed and none appears twice, so the file holds 25 rows and\n25 distinct landforms."},{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":10,"end_line":11,"quoted_text":"One row is: one rock glacier, surveyed once and summarised by a single mean creep velocity\nIndependent unit column: landform_id"}]},{"description":"By direct inspection of the input CSV, the 25 data rows carry landform_id values RG-01 through RG-25 with zero duplicates, so no independent unit contributes more than one row to the row-independent procedure.","observed_value":"25 unique landform_id values (RG-01..RG-25), 12 micaschist rows and 13 orthogneiss rows","source_spans":[{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":1,"end_line":2,"quoted_text":"landform_id,bedrock_class,crest_elevation_m,mean_slope_deg,creep_velocity_cm_yr\nRG-01,micaschist,2685,17.4,24.7"},{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":26,"end_line":26,"quoted_text":"RG-25,orthogneiss,2678,18.9,16.0"}]},{"description":"The workflow enforces uniqueness of the independent-unit column before computing any statistics, raising an error if any landform_id repeats; the Welch t-test therefore runs only on data guaranteed to have one row per unit.","observed_value":"uniqueness guard on landform_id precedes stats.ttest_ind","source_spans":[{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":39,"end_line":41,"quoted_text":"ids = [row[UNIT_COL] for row in rows]\n    if len(set(ids)) != len(ids):\n        raise ValueError(\"landform_id must be unique: one row per landform\")"},{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":62,"end_line":62,"quoted_text":"result = stats.ttest_ind(x, y, equal_var=False)"}]},{"description":"The report's design section and selected result accurately claim one row per landform and 25 independent observations, matching the data.","observed_value":"reported n = 12 + 13 = 25 equals the number of distinct landforms","source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":5,"end_line":7,"quoted_text":"Each row of `data/input.csv` is one rock glacier, surveyed once. No landform\ncontributes more than one row, so the 25 velocity values are 25 independent\nobservations."},{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":25,"end_line":25,"quoted_text":"[selected-result] Welch two-sided t-test: micaschist-hosted rock glaciers creep 8.00 cm/yr faster than orthogneiss-hosted ones (24.00 vs 16.00 cm/yr; t = 4.06, df = 19.8, p < 0.001, Cohen's d = 1.65), one row per landform."}]}],"counterevidence_atoms":[{"description":"Searched for any sign that an independent unit enters the procedure repeatedly (duplicate landform_id values, resurveys, row expansion or replication in the workflow) and found none; the reported group sizes, means, SDs, and Welch statistics (n = 12 vs 13, 24.00 vs 16.00 cm/yr, SD 5.63 vs 4.01, t = 4.06, df = 19.8, p < 0.001, d = 1.65) all reproduce from the 25-row CSV under one-row-per-landform analysis, leaving no unexplained inflation of effective sample size.","observed_value":"hand recomputation from data/input.csv reproduces all reported statistics; no duplication mechanism exists in workflow/analysis.py","source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":13,"end_line":14,"quoted_text":"| micaschist | 12 | 24.00 | 5.63 |\n| orthogneiss | 13 | 16.00 | 4.01 |"},{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":21,"end_line":23,"quoted_text":"Difference in means (micaschist - orthogneiss): 8.00 cm/yr\nt = 4.06, Welch-Satterthwaite df = 19.8, p < 0.001\nCohen's d (pooled SD) = 1.65"},{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":48,"end_line":52,"quoted_text":"def velocities(label):\n        return np.array(\n            [float(row[VALUE_COL]) for row in rows if row[GROUP_COL] == label],\n            dtype=float,\n        )"}]}],"falsification_attempt":"I attempted to demonstrate the issue by (1) scanning all 25 landform_id values in data/input.csv for duplicates (none: RG-01 through RG-25 each appear exactly once), (2) checking the workflow for any code path that could replicate rows or aggregate repeated surveys into the test (there is none; a guard raises ValueError on duplicate IDs before stats.ttest_ind is called), and (3) recomputing the group counts, means, standard deviations, Welch t statistic, Welch-Satterthwaite df, and Cohen's d by hand from the CSV. All recomputed values (n = 12/13, means 24.00/16.00, SD 5.63/4.01, t = 4.06, df = 19.8, d = 1.65, p < 0.001) match the report, so the selected result is consistent with exactly one entry per independent unit and the issue could not be demonstrated.","cross_case_evidence_used":false,"unresolved_material_questions":[],"self_reported_confidence":"high"}]},"ttft_ms":33769,"ttft_stream_ms":1766,"time_to_request_ms":15,"type":"result","duration_ms":76270,"uuid":"3c81d7e7-8e35-4093-a095-6b8d992ad979"}
